Six symbols CMake needs that this port declared or implied and never defined.

EVERY ONE OF THESE BINDS LAZILY, which is what made them expensive to find: an absent symbol does
not fail at launch, it aborts inside dyld_stub_binder the first time a caller reaches it, with
signal 6 at a dyld frame and nothing naming the framework. DYLD_BIND_AT_LAUNCH=1 turns that into
"Symbol not found: _<name>" at startup, one at a time, which is how this list was built.

  CGColorSpaceCopyPropertyList   NULL is a legal answer on macOS too for a space with no property
                                 list form; an absent symbol is not.
  CGPathCreateWithRoundedRect    Built from the arcs CGPath.m already has. The radii are CLAMPED TO
                                 HALF THE SIDE, as CoreGraphics does, because a corner wider than
                                 the rectangle wraps the arcs past each other into a self
                                 intersecting path. A zero radius degenerates to the plain rect.
  CGEventTapCreateForPid         Delegates to CGEventTapCreate. Nothing here distinguishes taps by
                                 pid, and pretending to filter would be worse than not filtering.
  CGSSetWindowTags               Declared in CoreGraphicsPrivate.h and never defined. Window tags
  CGSClearWindowTags             are a presentation hint the window server keeps, and there is no
                                 window server here. They answer SUCCESS: a caller told its hint
                                 failed may decide the window is unusable, while a caller whose hint
                                 is quietly not honoured cannot tell us from a server that ignored
                                 it.
  NSBitsPerSampleFromDepth       Arithmetic, not a table: the depth constants carry bits per sample
  NSColorSpaceFromDepth          in their low byte (0x208 is 8, 0x210 is 16, 0x220 is 32), and all
                                 three depths this port offers are RGB.

MEASURED: with these and CFURLEnumeratorCreateForMountedVolumes in place, CMake launches under
DYLD_BIND_AT_LAUNCH=1 with NO missing symbol at all, where before it named one, then the next, then
the next.

--- a/AppKit/NSScreen.m
+++ b/AppKit/NSScreen.m
@@ -200,3 +200,19 @@
 }
 
 @end
+
+/*
+ * THE DEPTH CONSTANTS ENCODE BITS PER SAMPLE IN THEIR LOW BYTE, which is why these are arithmetic
+ * rather than a table: NSWindowDepthTwentyfourBitRGB is 0x208 and carries 8, the sixty four bit one
+ * 0x210 carries 16, the hundred and twenty eight bit one 0x220 carries 32. Task #234.
+ */
+NSInteger NSBitsPerSampleFromDepth(NSWindowDepth depth)
+{
+    return (NSInteger)(depth & 0xFF);
+}
+
+/* All three depths this port offers are RGB; there is no grey or CMYK window depth among them. */
+NSString *NSColorSpaceFromDepth(NSWindowDepth depth)
+{
+    return NSCalibratedRGBColorSpace;
+}
